{0 mls}

[mls] implements the Messaging Layer Security protocol
({{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9420.html}RFC 9420}) in OCaml, building
on the [hpke] package for RFC 9180 operations.

The entry point for applications is {!Mls.Group}: create a group with
{!Mls.Group.create}, add members by committing {!Mls.Proposal.Add} proposals
built from their {!Mls.Key_package}s, join from a Welcome with
{!Mls.Group.join} or from a GroupInfo with {!Mls.Group.external_join}, and
exchange {!Mls.Mls_message} values through {!Mls.Group.process},
{!Mls.Group.val-commit}, and {!Mls.Group.encrypt_application}. Every operation
returns a new state rather than mutating the old one.

{1 Modules}

{2 Application interface}

{!modules: Mls.Group Mls.Key_package Mls.Leaf_node Mls.Credential
Mls.Capabilities Mls.Mls_message Mls.Proposal Mls.Psk Mls.Extension
Mls.Group_extensions Mls.Cipher_suite Mls.Crypto Mls.Error}

{2 Protocol internals}

{!modules: Mls.Ratchet_tree Mls.Treekem Mls.Key_schedule Mls.Secret_tree
Mls.Transcript_hash Mls.Message_protection Mls.Framing Mls.Group_context
Mls.Group_info Mls.Welcome Mls.Commit Mls.Update_path Mls.Node
Mls.Parent_node Mls.Hpke_ciphertext Mls.Tree_math Mls.Tls Mls.Hex}

{1 Cipher suites}

Suites 0x0001, 0x0002, 0x0003, 0x0005 and 0x0007 are supported. Suites
0x0004 and 0x0006 require X448 and Ed448, which are not available in OCaml;
they are recognised on the wire but cannot be used.

{1 Security}

The library is unaudited. See the repository's SECURITY.md for the threat
model, the checks performed on received messages, and known limitations.
